<title>FINLAND: Partek jumps on Sisu merger news.</title>
<headline>Partek jumps on Sisu merger news.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Finnish cargo handling equipment and building materials group Partek Oy Ab rose sharply on Wednesday after the group announced a merger with state-controlled truck builder Sisu.</p>
<p>At 1440/1240 GMT Partek traded at 82.00 markka, up 6.00 markka or almost eight percent, in lively 20 million markka turnover.</p>
<p>Brokers said the share rose clearly on the news, but they were reluctant to comment immediately.</p>
<p>&quot;This is quite an unusual merger,&quot; one broker said.</p>
<p>--John Acher, Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 235</p>
